# SQL Injection UNION Attack: Finding a Column Containing Text

> **PortSwigger Web Security Academy Lab** demonstrating how to identify a column capable of displaying string values using a UNION-based SQL Injection.

---

# Overview

This lab demonstrates how to identify which column in a SQL query can display text values. Before sensitive data can be extracted using a UNION-based SQL Injection, it is necessary to determine both the number of columns returned by the original query and which column supports string data.

---

# Objective

- Determine the number of columns returned by the query
- Identify a column that accepts string values
- Display arbitrary text within the application's response
- Complete the lab using a UNION-based SQL Injection

